  "ordinary_statement_and_proof_fidelity": [
    "Row3Granular states the semantic bound Q(A)<=sqrt(3/2) C(A) for every three-row sign matrix and every real inner-product space, with sSup-defined vector and scalar optima. It explicitly treats an empty vector-feasible set.",
    "Its proof uses the four projective column-type weights, scalar sign anchors, the parallelogram/Parseval identity and Cauchy-Schwarz; it does not assume or compute an exact C optimum.",
    "SemanticTestGranular gives four individual fixed-matrix sqrt(2) bounds, dimensions6x6,6x8,7x8,8x8. Each uses an explicit positive sum-of-squares dual certificate and a scalar sign-witness lower anchor; it does not prove an exhaustive all-size family or the unrestricted Grothendieck conjecture.",
    "The four numerical certificates have (Cnum,U)=(14,19),(20,27),(22,31),(28,77/2); their exact threshold comparisons are361<=392,729<=800,961<=968,5929<=6272.",
    "The semantic theorems and exact certificates are held pending their original-route fresh replay and bounded prior-work/coverage review. This inspection does not assign originality or change a score."
  ],
